CAT = "aesiraPowers"; SEG = "POW"
Q = [
("A private guard in Dubai has the same powers as a police officer:",
 "Never", ["Inside the client's site", "At night only", "After five years' service"],
 "A SIRA licence gives no police powers. Guards observe, deter and report, and act within what any person may lawfully do."),
("A guard sees a man snatch a handbag in a mall and catches him. What must the guard do next?",
 "Hand him to police quickly", ["Hold him until the next day", "Take his ID and let him go", "Search his phone for evidence"],
 "UAE criminal procedure lets anyone who witnesses an offence as it happens take the offender to the nearest police. Holding him longer than needed is unlawful detention."),
("While waiting for police with a detained shoplifter, the guard should:",
 "Keep them safe and watched", ["Lock them in a store room alone", "Question them for a confession", "Photograph them for social media"],
 "The guard is responsible for the person's safety until police arrive. Confessions are for police, and posting images breaches privacy."),
("How much force may a guard use when lawfully restraining someone?",
 "Only what is necessary", ["As much as the guard wishes", "Force matching the item's value", "Any force once they resist"],
 "Force must be the minimum needed in the circumstances and stop once the threat ends. Excessive force can be a criminal offence."),
("A guard is attacked with a fist. The guard's response in self-defence must be:",
 "Proportionate to the attack", ["As strong as possible", "Delayed until the next day", "Carried out with any weapon to hand"],
 "UAE law recognises legitimate defence, but the response must be proportionate. Continuing after the danger has ended is no longer defence."),
("A drunk man stops resisting and lies still on the floor. What should the guard do with the restraint?",
 "Ease it and check his breathing", ["Increase the pressure to be safe", "Sit on his chest to hold him", "Leave him face down alone"],
 "Once resistance ends, force must reduce. Pressure on the chest or a face-down position can stop breathing, so the guard monitors him closely."),
("May a guard carry a baton or pepper spray on duty in Dubai?",
 "Only if licensed for it", ["Yes, any guard may carry them", "Yes, if bought abroad", "Yes, if the client agrees"],
 "Defensive tools are controlled security materials. They may be carried only under the licence type, SIRA approval and the employer's procedure."),
("A shopper refuses to show their receipt at a store exit. A guard who suspects theft but saw nothing should:",
 "Let them go and report it", ["Block the exit by force", "Search their bags anyway", "Take their car keys from them"],
 "Without seeing an offence, the guard has no grounds to detain or search. Noting a description and informing the police or the store is lawful."),
("A guard wants to search a suspected thief's pockets. When is this lawful?",
 "With the person's consent", ["Whenever the guard is sure", "If the item is expensive", "If the person is a tourist"],
 "Guards have no power to search people against their will. Without consent, the guard waits for the police, who have that power."),
("A guard takes a photo of a woman arguing in a lobby and shares it in a group chat. This may be:",
 "A breach of UAE privacy law", ["Allowed as shared evidence", "Good security team practice", "Required by SIRA rules"],
 "Photographing and sharing images of people without consent can breach UAE privacy laws. Evidence is kept and passed to police, not shared."),
("A man refuses to leave a private residential building after the guard asks him to. What should the guard do?",
 "Call the police if he stays", ["Drag him outside the building", "Lock him in the lobby", "Threaten him with a baton"],
 "The guard asks politely and explains. If the person refuses, the police deal with it; dragging or locking someone in can be assault or unlawful detention."),
("A guard may restrain a person, if needed, mainly to:",
 "Prevent harm to anyone", ["Get a written apology", "Recover a parking fee", "Make the person show ID"],
 "Physical intervention is a last resort to stop injury or a serious offence in progress, never to collect fees or identification."),
("A guard catches a teenager writing graffiti on a wall. Which action is lawful and safe?",
 "Stop it and call the police", ["Fine the teenager on the spot", "Keep the teenager's phone", "Make them repaint the wall now"],
 "Guards cannot issue fines or confiscate property. They stop the damage if safe, keep the person in sight and pass the matter to the police."),
("A guard handcuffs a person to a railing and goes on patrol. Why is this wrong?",
 "It is unsafe and unlawful", ["Railings may be damaged", "Handcuffs need a daily check", "Patrols must be kept shorter"],
 "A detained person must be supervised at all times. Leaving them restrained and alone risks injury and goes beyond any lawful detention."),
("A guard is told by a client to hold a suspected fraudster in an office until the morning. The guard should:",
 "Refuse and call the police", ["Agree, as the client pays", "Hold them but feed them", "Hold them until they confess"],
 "Only the police and courts may detain people for long periods. A guard who holds someone overnight risks committing unlawful detention."),
("A guard sees a man punch another man in a car park. What is the first priority?",
 "Safety of people, then call 999", ["Taking photos to use as evidence", "Writing the report first", "Asking the men to shake hands"],
 "Preserve life and safety first, calling the police on 999. Notes and evidence follow once people are safe."),
("A guard suspects a guest is using illegal drugs in a hotel room. The guard should:",
 "Report it to the supervisor", ["Enter and search the room", "Seize the guest's passport", "Warn the guest to hide it"],
 "Searching rooms and seizing passports are police matters. The guard reports what was seen through the proper route."),
("A person drops a fake banknote at a till and the cashier calls the guard. The guard should:",
 "Keep it safe and call police", ["Return it to the person politely", "Tear it up in front of them", "Spend it to test it"],
 "Suspected counterfeit currency is evidence. It is handled as little as possible, kept safe and handed to the police."),
("Which statement about a guard's use of handcuffs is correct?",
 "Only if trained and authorised", ["Any guard may use them", "They may be used as punishment", "They replace calling police"],
 "Restraint equipment is used only by guards trained and authorised for it, as a safety measure, and the police are called at once."),
("A guard who sees an offence but is not sure of the facts should:",
 "Report what was seen", ["Detain everyone nearby", "Decide guilt and punish", "Ignore it to avoid mistakes"],
 "When the facts are unclear, the guard records and reports what was observed. Investigating and deciding guilt is for the police."),
]
